{"annotations": [], "blocks": [{"bbox": [49.305000000000064, 75.029, 290.25300000000027, 229.77727770177876], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 0, "source": "docling", "text": "Eÿcacy outcomes were analyzed using a modified intentionto-treat (mITT) principle. The analysis population, referred to as the full analysis set (FAS), included all randomized patients who received at least one dose of the study intervention and provided at least one post-baseline eÿcacy assessment. Missing data for the primary outcome were handled using multiple imputation, and analyses were conducted on fi ve imputed datasets (Supplementary File 3). Continuous variables were reported as mean with standard deviation (SD) and compared using either Student's t -test or the Wilcoxon rank-sum test. Categorical variables were summarized as frequencies and percentages, and analyzed using the chi-square test, Fisher's exact test or MannWhitney U -test, as appropriate."}, {"bbox": [49.30500000000015, 234.3830000000005, 290.25300000000016, 303.3229012345686], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 1, "source": "docling", "text": "The primary outcome-change in VAS score from baseline to Week 12-was analyzed using a generalized linear model, with adjustments for baseline VAS score, study center, and rescue medication use, and the interaction between center and treatment. Secondary outcomes were assessed for statistically significant dierences from baseline to Week 24. The safety set (SS), which included all participants who received at least one dose of the intervention, was used for all safety analyses."}, {"bbox": [304.4099999999999, 99.65300000000082, 545.3670000000003, 193.6759012345691], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 2, "source": "docling", "text": "A key sensitivity analysis was conducted based on the perprotocol set (PPS), which included participants who completed the 12-week intervention and had no major protocol violations. Prespecified subgroup analyses were also conducted based on sex, age ( ≤ 65 vs. > 65 years), and CCS grade (I-II vs. III). All statistical tests were two-tailed, and a P -value < 0.05 was considered statistically significant. Analyses were carried out using SPSS 18.0 (IBM SPSS Inc., Armonk, NY, United States)."}, {"bbox": [304.425, 229.85400000000004, 360.27450000000005, 242.36850000000004], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 3, "source": "docling", "text": "3 Results"}, {"bbox": [304.4229999999999, 258.71299999999997, 545.3710000000001, 303.379901234568], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 4, "seq": 4, "source": "docling", "text": "Between June 2020 and June 2022, a total of 263 individuals were screened across six tertiary hospitals in China, of whom 152 were deemed enrolled and randomized. Four patients (2.6%, two in each group) were excluded from the FAS because they did not"}], "checksum": "b6bea03bdd584bc2c8d6653a15256eaa800cb146e0f94d17cbaa358d07628f46", "content_present": true, "doc_id": "d-e546a005ed1bb895", "docling_version": "2.118.0", "engine_version": "2.118.0", "errors": [], "images": [{"bbox": [48.5537544215098, 320.3775181199496, 546.3763143733144, 777.9757570489497], "blob": "", "caption": "", "checksum": "8b4c6432a517edc04df78215dc731b24ad7dad552cd08890ad1e6a98e7ead972", "mime": "image/png", "page": 4, "storage_ref": ""}], "page_index": 3, "page_sizes": {"4": [595.2760009765625, 841.8900146484375]}, "route": "docling", "schema_version": "v0.1.0", "source_hash": "e546a005ed1bb8957707c4a76f66c3aea22f3a70c49f1649ed76f2f4c6a4e94e", "status": "ok", "tables": [], "timings": {}}